{"rank": 77, "article": "Ted Lasso", "revid": 1154195452, "parentid": 1154180342, "user": "Drovethrughosts", "timestamp": "2023-05-10T21:38:44Z", "comment": "Undid revision 1154180342 by [[Special:Contributions/2600:6C5C:6A00:D62:345E:BEA0:BF0A:C15D|2600:6C5C:6A00:D62:345E:BEA0:BF0A:C15D]] ([[User talk:2600:6C5C:6A00:D62:345E:BEA0:BF0A:C15D|talk]] [[WP:SYNTH]] from the source; an IP has been trying to push Terry Smith into this article, please see talk page for prior incidents", "tags": ["mw-undo", "wikieditor"], "size": 110213}
{"rank": 77, "article": "Ted Lasso", "revid": 1154180342, "parentid": 1154119016, "user": "2600:6C5C:6A00:D62:345E:BEA0:BF0A:C15D", "timestamp": "2023-05-10T19:33:31Z", "comment": "/* Development */ Provides factual evidence that the Lasso writers and actors researched Terry Smith and knew a considerable amount about Smith. In fact, many of the Ted Lasso storylines were taken directly from 1990’s media coverage of Smith. For example, in Episode 3 of Season 1, Lasso’s school visit is identical to a BBC television documentary about Smith, and the newspaper article written about Lasso in episode 3 uses exact wording from a 12/13/99 Manchester Evening News article about Smith.", "tags": ["mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 111013}
{"rank": 77, "article": "Ted Lasso", "revid": 1154119016, "parentid": 1154117670, "user": "Drovethrughosts", "timestamp": "2023-05-10T11:17:54Z", "comment": "", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 110213}
